      "description": "Watch FC Augsburg vs Bayer Leverkusen highlights and goals from Bundesliga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 12, 2026. The atmosphere at the WWK Arena was electric as FC Augsburg and Bayer Leverkusen prepared for a Bundesliga clash that promised high-octane action. On September 12, 2026, fans were treated to a showcase of tactical adjustments and individual brilliance that kept the outcome in doubt until the final whistle. Leverkusen Take the Initiative The visitors started with clear intent, dominating possession and pinning the hosts back. In the 18th minute, the pressure told when Edmond Tapsoba found Christian Kofane , who clinicaly finished with his left foot to give Bayer Leverkusen the lead. Throughout the first half, Aleix Garcia was the primary architect, swinging in numerous corners that tested the Augsburg defense, though the hosts managed to keep the deficit to a single goal heading into the break. The Gregoritsch Turnaround The second half saw a dramatic shift in momentum as Augsburg emerged with renewed energy. In the 50th minute, Michael Gregoritsch drew the sides level after being set up by Hennes Behrens . The turnaround was completed just five minutes later when Michael Gregoritsch struck again, this time powering home a header from a Fabian Rieder corner. The quickfire double stunned the visitors and shifted the pressure back onto the reigning contenders. VAR Drama and Schick's Stunning Finale The final half-hour was filled with tension and officiating drama. Bayer Leverkusen thought they had equalized in the 61st minute, but a lengthy VAR review led to the goal being overturned for a prior foul. Tempers flared, leading to yellow cards for dissent and violent conduct. Just as it looked like Augsburg would secure a famous victory, Patrik Schick produced a moment of magic in the 89th minute. Assisted by Malik Tillman , the striker scored a sensational back-heeled goal to rescue a 2-2 draw. Despite late chances for Moussa Diaby in stoppage time, both teams had to settle for a hard-fought point."
